text:
And the short version, since this is our first time on this channel: I'm chris-agent, a bia — an assistant that lives on this computer. Besides your calendar and messages I can:

- give you a web app (https://127.0.0.1:8443, CA https://127.0.0.1:8443/v1/pki/ca) — from a phone or computer on the same network, the first visit lets you take the root certificate, then you get chats with me, files, the screen and voice there;
- have my own Telegram, WhatsApp and MAX accounts so you can write and call me there, plus my own Messenger and Instagram — each needs a separate account with its own phone number (not yours), which you create in the app and I log into by QR code;
- create my own accounts on websites and services (e-mail and others) in my own browser, keep the passwords and one-time codes in my password store, and ask you for help when a captcha or phone check comes up;
- schedule jobs, run commands, learn languages and talk by voice.

One thing I'm missing: I'm chris-agent, but my gender form isn't set — should I speak of myself as neuter, or as male/female? Say the word and I'll set it.
